@startuml fig-3-3-erd-physical
' Figure 3.3 — Physical schema as implemented
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
hide circle

entity "scans" as scans {
  * id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  * url : TEXT <<IX ix_scans_url>>
  * verdict : VARCHAR(20)
  * risk_score : DOUBLE PRECISION
  * risk_pct : INTEGER
  * confidence_pct : INTEGER
  client_id : VARCHAR(64) <<IX ix_scans_client_id>>
  --
  url_features : JSONB
  network_signals : JSONB
  permission_signals : JSONB
  scam_content_signals : JSONB
  shap_values : JSONB
  flagged_rules : JSONB
  --
  * created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
  * last_scanned_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
}

entity "alembic_version" as av {
  * version_num : VARCHAR(32) <<PK>>
}

note right of scans
  Six nullable JSONB columns collapse the seven
  satellite entities of Figure 3.2 (scam_content_
  signals added by revision 762a960b07ca, after
  the page-content scanner landed).

  Justification (ADR-007):
  - Attribution arrays are variable length and
    always read as a whole with their parent row;
    no query filters on an individual attribution.
  - The feature set changes whenever the model is
    retrained. A normalised column-per-feature
    schema would require a migration per retrain.
  - PostgreSQL JSONB is indexable via GIN if a
    query pattern later demands it, so the
    decision is reversible.

  client_id (revision 4d6f5fb287b2) is nullable and
  indexed, not a foreign key to any USER-type
  entity: it scopes /history and /stats to one
  browser install, deliberately not an account.
  risk_pct (33be02683ae4) and last_scanned_at
  (f48ff135cc1a) are later additions, per ADR-015
  and the upsert-by-(client_id, url) behaviour.

  Cost, stated plainly: referential integrity for
  rule flags is enforced in application code rather
  than by a foreign key.
end note
@enduml
